  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Initiative for Enhancing Migration Law and Policy through a Network of Legal Experts on Migration for West and Central Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is the contribution of Switzerland to a multi-donor 3-year Initiative of IOM that seeks to establish a Network of Legal Experts on Migration for West and Central Africa to drive substantial positive change in migration law and policies in the region. This network gathers esteemed legal professionals from WCA, fostering a platform for high-quality legal analysis, discussion and representation. This expert network is expected to play a crucial role in fortifying regional solutions, adhering to international law, incorporating local insights and global standards. It aims to become an independent, influential entity, deeply rooted in a robust organizational structure. The project contributes to two main outcomes. The first outcome involves establishing the Network as a key independent legal actor in WCA. This includes forming a Steering Committee, expanding membership based on competitive selection, ensuring diverse and gender-sensitive representation, and registering the Network as a legal entity. This setup will enhance the Network&apos;s sustainability and enable active participation in various forums. The second outcome aims to gain recognition for the Network among key stakeholders, positioning it as a primary reference for informed migration law and policy formulation. This initiative will utilize a multifaceted approach to build relationships and coordinate systematically between regional legal and policy experts, through evidence-based and rights-based approaches. Ultimately, the project aims to foster a coherent, inclusive, and responsive migration policy landscape in WCA, leveraging the expertise of the Network to influence decision-makers and contribute to sustainable development in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
